+// within its window, lowThreshold otherwise. This separates the GATING criterion
+// (single burst → short latch) from the EXTENSION criterion (repeated burst →
+// long latch), allowing poisson (isolated bursts) to benefit from short-latch
+// optimum and weibull (clustered bursts) to benefit from long-latch optimum.
